      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability issues:\n- Unused imports (`ArrayList`, `List`, `BiFunction`, `Function`, `Stream`, `DeprecatedAttributes`, parameterized test annotations)\n- Unused methods (`deprecatedAttributesData`, `assertEquivalent`) that create cognitive noise\n- The `underTest` variable is reused/reassigned, making the flow harder to follow\n- Missing assertion messages for some cases\n\nLet me write the improved test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes all unused imports and dead code (`deprecatedAttributesData`, `assertEquivalent`), renames the reused `underTest` variable into two clearly named `defaultFormatter` and `customFormatter` locals, and adds assertion messages to every `assertEquals` call for clarity."
